          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अधित्यका — adhityakā — \"a plateau; high table-land\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पर्वतस्य उपरि विशाला अधित्यका अस्ति। parvatasya upari viśālā adhityakā asti. On top of the mountain there is a wide plateau."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अधित्यका (adhityakā) is built on adhi, \"over, above\", through adhi-tya, as MW gives it (Pāṇini 5.2.34); MW gives adhityakā as land on the upper part of a mountain, table-land (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
